Add the opt-in --invariant-constructor-inference option. With the refreshed type system, a datatype constructor argument whose formal type uses a type parameter in a non-variant position, such as the tail of a list, fixes the constructor's type argument, so `Cons(h, ts)` with `h: int` and `ts: List<Pos>` checks `h` against `Pos` instead of requiring an inductive proof that `ts` is a `List<int>` (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/101).
